<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Automat Chem</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Automatic Chemistry</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0142-0453</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">18924892</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2547912</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pii">S1463924691000202</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/S1463924691000202</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Automatic system for the determination of boron in ceramic frits</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000e1;s</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Estela</surname><given-names>J. M.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Cerd&#x000e0;</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Ochandio</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff2">2</xref><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff3">3</xref></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="aff1"><label>1</label><addr-line>Department of Chemistry</addr-line><addr-line>University of the Balearic Islands</addr-line><addr-line>Palma de Mallorca</addr-line><addr-line>07071</addr-line><country>Spain</country></aff><aff id="aff2"><label>2</label><addr-line>Asociaci&#x000f3;n Espa&#x000f1;ola de Industrias Cer&#x000e1;micas (AICE), Paterna</addr-line><addr-line>Valencia</addr-line><country>Spain</country></aff><aff id="aff3"><label>3</label><addr-line>Instituto Technol&#x000f3;gico Cer&#x000e1;mico (ITC)</addr-line><addr-line>Universidad de Valencia</addr-line><country>Spain</country></aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>1991</year></pub-date><volume>13</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1991 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1991</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract><p>An automatic system for the potentiometric determination of boronin ceramic frits was developed. The system includes a personal computer for instrumental control, data acquisition and processing, which allows up to 13 samples to be analysed sequentially with no human intervention.</p><p>The system performance was tested on the titration of standard solutions, which it carried out with low errors and RSD. It was subsequently applied to the determination of the B<sub>2</sub>0<sub>3</sub> content in various types of ceramic frits with good results.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>